</style></head><body><main><h1>Canvas Help Queue Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Effective date: November 2, 2026<br>Applies to: Canvas Help Queue extension version 0.6.1</p>
<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>Canvas Help Queue processes Canvas discussion data locally to display a classroom help queue. It does not transmit student data to the extension developer or third-party services. Completion records and preferences are stored locally in the browser.</p>
<p>The extension connects to your Canvas website to retrieve discussion data. It is not an offline application.</p>
<h2>Data accessed</h2>
<p>When you open the extension on a Canvas course discussion, it uses your existing Canvas session to read:</p>
<ul><li>Your Canvas profile information, including your account identifier and display name, to identify the signed-in account.</li><li>The selected discussion's title, course and discussion identifiers, and discussion settings.</li><li>Discussion replies, including participants' display names and identifiers, post identifiers, message content, and posting dates and times.</li></ul>
<p>This information is used to identify help requests, separate today's requests from earlier requests, display the waiting order, and update the queue when replies change or disappear. The extension does not request your password or require you to supply an API token.</p>
<h2>Processing and display</h2>
<p>Request matching, spelling tolerance, date filtering, queue ordering, and sound playback run in your browser. Participant names, message text, and posting dates are processed in memory; the extension does not write those fields to its persistent local storage.</p>
<p>If you open the projector window, the extension passes waiting names and post identifiers to that window through internal extension messages. People who can see the projector can see the displayed names and queue positions. Discussion message text is displayed in the teacher panel, not the projector roster.</p>
<p>The extension does not enter grades, change discussion replies, or mark Canvas posts as read. Checking a completion box changes the extension's local completion record.</p>
<h2>Data saved on your device</h2>
<p>The extension uses local extension storage for:</p>
<ul><li>Completion records containing the Canvas site, signed-in account identifier, course identifier, discussion identifier, post identifier, and completion time. These identifiers may be linked to people or activity within Canvas.</li><li>Preferences such as matching options, refresh interval, sound settings, and volume.</li><li>Your selected projector character.</li><li>The filename and contents of an audio file you choose for notifications.</li></ul>
<p>These records remain in the browser profile until removed. The extension does not use browser sync storage to synchronize them between devices or browsers. Firefox and Edge keep separate records.</p>
<h2>Network connections and sharing</h2>
<p>The extension makes read-only requests to the Canvas site you are using to retrieve your profile, the selected discussion, and its replies. It uses the permissions and existing login of the signed-in Canvas account. Canvas and your institution handle those requests under their own policies.</p>
<p>The extension has no developer-operated server, analytics service, advertising service, or remote error-reporting service. It does not upload queue data, completion records, preferences, or custom audio to the extension developer or a third-party service. It does not sell student data or use it for advertising.</p>
<p>Your browser, operating system, and Canvas may perform their own logging, updates, backups, or other processing independently of the extension. This policy describes the extension's behavior.</p>
<h2>Permissions</h2>
<ul><li><strong>activeTab:</strong> Grants temporary access to the tab where you click the extension so it can open the discussion queue.</li><li><strong>scripting:</strong> Allows the extension to run its bundled queue interface in that tab.</li><li><strong>storage:</strong> Saves completion records, preferences, character selection, and optional custom audio locally.</li></ul>
<p>The extension does not request general access to your browsing history or blanket permission to read every website.</p>
<h2>Retention and removal</h2>
<p>Closing the source tab or stopping the queue ends that queue's processing and display; the extension does not preserve the names or messages in a local queue database. Earlier requests are retrieved again from Canvas when you reopen the queue.</p>
<p>Unchecking a completed request removes its local completion record. Choosing <strong>Use default chime</strong> removes the saved custom audio file. To remove all extension-managed records, clear the extension's local storage using the browser's extension controls or remove the extension. Browser behavior may affect when removal finishes.</p>
<p>Removing extension data does not delete any Canvas discussion posts or other Canvas records.</p>
<h2>Changes and contact</h2>
<p>This policy will be updated if the extension's data practices change. Publisher contact information is available through the extension's developer profile on Microsoft Edge Add-ons.</p></main></body></html>
